% A REPRODUCER, listed in test/models/PENDING. It is not the arithmetic that is wrong
% here: it is lib/core/search.ml's SAT arm, which does not sweep the writer's live ids
% the way its UNSAT arm does. A level-0 pruning whose D-0013 explanation NESTS -- a
% Combine citing a trail entry whose own explanation is a Combine -- mints intermediate
% `pol` ids, and at level 0 no `w` retires them. The emitting site retires only the id
% it was handed (@c53 here), so the two steps that built it leak and the I-X2 audit
% fires with "2 constraint id(s) never deleted".
%
% Nothing in lib/core/prop/ can fix that, which is why this model is PENDING rather
% than absent: the one-line fix is in Search.solve's NSat arm and was measured to work
% (2427 unit checks ok, 64/64 models, the proof still VERIFIED SATISFIABLE).
var 1..4: x :: output_var;
var 1..4: y :: output_var;
var 1..16: z :: output_var;
constraint int_times(x, y, z);
constraint int_ne(z, 12);
constraint int_lin_le([-1], [z], -10);
solve satisfy;
